    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.T — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.T#\n\n- property DataFrame.T[source]#\n- The transpose of the DataFrame. This property returns a DataFrame with rows and columns interchanged, reflecting the data across the main diagonal. \n  - Returns:\n    - DataFrame\n    - The transposed DataFrame.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.transpose`\n  - Transpose index and columns.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"col1\": [1, 2], \"col2\": [3, 4]}) >>> df col1 col2 0 1 3 1 2 4 >>> df.T 0 1 col1 1 2 col2 3 4",
    "markdown_length": 462,
